{{!--
  One socket of the Overview figure (D-689, redrawn to WoW's own character
  pane 2026-09-20): a slot, and what is worn or held in it.

  **THE SOCKET CARRIES NO WORDS.** The lead's reference is WoW's paper doll -
  eight square icon-only sockets down each side of the figure and a row of
  them beneath - so the icon in its rarity ring IS the tile. What it is is
  said twice instead, and both are composed in `#overview`: in the
  `aria-label`, which names the SLOT and then what is in it, and in the
  tooltip, which is the Gear tab's own card through `rules/bags.mjs#tipModel`
  (`data-tooltip-html` for a filled socket, the plain `data-tooltip` for an
  empty one; the class comes off the `data-tooltip-class` on the figure).

  **AN EMPTY SOCKET IS WoW's OWN SILHOUETTE** for that slot, from the pinned
  paper-doll textures - `_overview.scss` keys it on `data-slot` - so an empty
  Head reads as a helm and an empty Feet as a boot without a word on either.

  **THE WHOLE TILE IS ONE CONTROL.** Filled or empty, it carries
  `data-action="pickSlot"`, and the picker lists only what the character is
  already carrying for that slot - never the compendium browser (the lead,
  2026-09-09). A RIGHT CLICK is the second door (`itemContextMenu`): Edit,
  Unequip, Star and the rest, the same menu a bag tile takes. There is no
  double-click, because the single click already opens the picker.

  **`data-slot` is on the tile itself**, because it is the drop zone as well
  as the control - `dropZoneOf` answers by kind and `#dropOnSlot` refuses
  anything the slot does not take, by name. A finger or a trinket draws two
  tiles off one slot key, so those carry `data-index` too and a drop on
  Finger 2 replaces what is in Finger 2.

  **A barred Off hand carries NO action** (D-689): an exclusively two-handed
  main hand leaves nothing for a shield, an Augment or a second blade, so
  neither the picker nor a drop may reach the tile. It is greyed AND said in
  words - the sentence is printed under the hands row by `overview.hbs`,
  because a tooltip nobody hovers is not a refusal.

  **There is no per-tile Unequip.** Twenty of them crowded the tab; *Take it
  off* is the first row of the picker now.

  It is a plate with a plain border and no `clip-path`: D11 SS9's bevelled
  octagons cut off every element hung outside them, twice.
--}}
{{!-- No `is-mirrored`: the right column's plates used to run words-then-icon
      so both columns' text faced the portrait, and a socket has no words to
      turn round. --}}
<div class="azeroth-slot-tile {{#if tile.filled}}is-filled{{else}}is-empty{{/if}}{{#if tile.barred}} is-barred{{/if}}"
     data-slot="{{tile.slot}}"{{#if tile.numbered}} data-index="{{tile.index}}"{{/if}}{{#if tile.id}} data-item-id="{{tile.id}}"{{/if}}
     aria-label="{{tile.ariaLabel}}"
     {{#if tile.tipHtml}}data-tooltip-html="{{tile.tipHtml}}"{{else}}data-tooltip="{{tile.tip}}"{{/if}}
     {{#if tile.barred}}role="button" aria-disabled="true"{{else if tile.editable}}data-action="pickSlot" role="button" tabindex="0"{{else}}role="img"{{/if}}>

  {{#if tile.filled}}
  {{> systems/azeroth-rpg/templates/actor/partials/item-icon.hbs img=tile.img rarityClass=tile.rarityClass}}
  {{/if}}
</div>
